# {{ display_name }} Install & Auth

## Overview
Set up {{ display_name }} SDK/CLI and configure authentication credentials.

## Prerequisites
- Node.js 18+ or Python 3.10+
- Package manager (npm, pnpm, or pip)
- {{ display_name }} account with API access
{% if category in ('ai-ml',) %}
- API key from {{ display_name }} dashboard (starts with `sk-` or similar prefix)
{% elif category in ('data-platform',) %}
- Database connection string or API key from {{ display_name }} dashboard
- Network access to database host (check firewall/VPC rules)
{% elif category in ('design-creative', 'sales-crm', 'enterprise-vertical') %}
- OAuth2 access token or personal API token from {{ display_name }} settings
{% else %}
- API key from {{ display_name }} dashboard
{% endif %}

## Instructions

### Step 1: Install SDK
```bash
# Node.js
npm install {{ npm_package | default(company + '-sdk') }}

# Python
pip install {{ pip_package | default(company) }}
```

### Step 2: Configure Authentication
{% if category in ('data-platform',) %}
```bash
# Set connection string (preferred for database platforms)
export {{ company | upper }}_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:pass@host:5432/db"

# Or use API key
export {{ company | upper }}_API_KEY="your-api-key"

# Or create .env file
cat >> .env << 'EOF'
{{ company | upper }}_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:pass@host:5432/db
{{ company | upper }}_API_KEY=your-api-key
EOF
```
{% elif category in ('design-creative',) %}
```bash
# OAuth2: Set access token (get from OAuth flow or personal tokens page)
export {{ company | upper }}_ACCESS_TOKEN="your-access-token"

# Or create .env file
echo '{{ company | upper }}_ACCESS_TOKEN=your-access-token' >> .env
```

> **Note:** OAuth tokens expire. For production, implement the refresh token flow.
> Personal access tokens (if available) are simpler for development.
{% else %}
```bash
# Set environment variable
export {{ company | upper }}_API_KEY="your-api-key"

# Or create .env file
echo '{{ company | upper }}_API_KEY=your-api-key' >> .env
```
{% endif %}

### Step 3: Verify Connection
```{{ primary_language | default('typescript') }}
{{ verification_code | default('// Test connection code here') }}
```

